@@ -812,6 +812,17 @@ Use ``--schema`` to include the schema of each table:
 
 The ``--nl``, ``--csv``, ``--tsv``, ``--table`` and ``--fmt`` options are also available.
 
+To restrict the output to specific tables, list their names after the database file. This is useful with ``--counts`` when your database contains very large tables, since it avoids counting rows in tables you are not interested in:
+
+.. code-block:: bash
+
+    sqlite-utils tables mydb.db dogs cats --counts
+
+.. code-block:: output
+
+    [{"table": "dogs", "count": 12},
+     {"table": "cats", "count": 332}]
+
 .. note::
     In Python: :ref:`db.tables or db.table_names() <python_api_tables>`  CLI reference: :ref:`sqlite-utils tables <cli_ref_tables>`
 
